From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "adnan.drina" <adnan.drina@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 3 Oct 2026 00:28:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] feat(compression): run-scoped compaction, request ceiling and
 pruned-stub refusal

RHOAI3 v32-qwen36, card t_2a95f8c1 run 44 (one Kanban turn, 97 API calls;
72K trigger, 48K prune, protect_last_n 12, context_length 110000): three
compaction passes (20:49:47, 20:55:12, 20:55:55Z) took 58-92 ms, removed no
message and summarised nothing. They used the per-turn attempt budget
(compression.max_attempts 3); the first armed the insufficient-progress
block; neither rearms until the provider reports a prompt below the trigger,
which never happened again. The real prompt grew to 121,375 tokens and the
next request waited out the 900 s stale timeout twice. Pruned write_file
arguments ("<200 chars>...[truncated]") were replayed as file content.

Why no summary (reproduced offline): in a single-turn run the only actionable
user message is the task that opens the transcript. After the first
compaction protect_first_n decays to 0, and the tail anchor "keep the last
user message in the tail" (#10896) pulls the tail back to that first message,
so the window holds only the previous handoff summary; compress() returns its
Phase-1 prune alone (empty_post_handoff_window). Live: 24->21, then 41->41,
67->67, 76->76.

With compression.run_scoped: true (agent/run_compaction.py), for the whole run:

- one pre-API guard replaces the per-turn-budgeted pre-API and post-tool gates
  (the turn-prologue preflight, the proactive prune and the provider-error
  handlers are unchanged): at or above threshold_tokens a pass runs; there is
  no attempt budget and no block, and after a pass the next one waits until
  the projected request has regrown by max(4096, 10% of the trigger);
- the opening task turn stays verbatim in the head (ContextCompressor
  _anchor_task_in_head), so a pass has a middle to summarise;
- a pass that summarised nothing while the request is still at or above the
  trigger is followed, before any request is sent, by a forced summarising
  pass with half the tail budget;
- ceiling: the projected prompt is the provider's last reported prompt count
  plus the rough size of what was added since, with a 25% margin on that
  addition only (a removal is credited at 75%); the rough whole-request
  estimate is used only before the first provider figure of the run. If the
  projection plus the output cap exceeds context_length, a forced pass runs
  regardless of runway, cooldown or anti-thrash state (half tail, then the
  minimum tail); if the request still does not fit, the run ends at once with
  context_ceiling_unreachable (Kanban: STOP WORKER_CONTEXT_CEILING) and the
  request is never sent.

Unconditionally: a pruned tool-call argument keeps its head and says what it
is ("[hermes pruned argument: N chars, first 200 shown; this is a context
stub, not the value that was sent]...[truncated]"; pruning a stub again
changes nothing), and write_file / patch refuse content that carries that
marker or the legacy 200-character "...[truncated]" stub, naming the reason;
nothing is written.

Without run_scoped every compaction path is unchanged. Local extension.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
